t calibrated values, but rank is per-frame so that's fine! So the premise hinges on WHAT PeakPickerIM emits as the 1/K0 of a picked cluster: apex-scan value (grid-aligned → rank == scan, modulo missing scans being skipped which doesn't matter for rank ordering... wait it does not matter: rank over distinct PRESENT values preserves order; two peaks from the same scan get same value → same rank; two peaks from different scans get different values → correct order. The rank is not the scan NUMBER but an order-preserving renumbering — for a tolerance in "scans", rank differences UNDERCOUNT scan differences when scans are missing (empty scans collapse). scan_tol derived from the same ranked values self-consistently uses the same collapsed coordinates — mostly consistent!) vs intensity-weighted centroid (grid-free → rank is just a total order of arbitrary floats; "scan" is meaningless, and cross-frame rank instability appears).

